{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionProtocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"PointerWrapper","preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib14PointerWrapperP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The end object must appear after the start object in the accessibility tree,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"i.e. the end object must be reachable from the start object by navigating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forward (next, first child etc)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This struct also contains a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_is_active"},{"type":"text","text":" boolean, to communicate if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of the selection is the active point or not."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The active point corresponds to the user’s focus or point of interest. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"user moves the active point to expand or collapse the range. The anchor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point is the other point of the range and typically remains constant. In"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most cases, anchor is the start of the range and active is the end. However,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when selecting backwards (e.g. pressing shift+left arrow in a text field),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the start of the range is the active point, as the user moves this to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"manipulate the selection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AtkTextSelection"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelection"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionRef"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/atk\/textselectionprotocol"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Atk\/4GLib14PointerWrapperP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelection","doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionRef"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This structure represents a single  text selection within a document. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection is defined by two points in the content, where each one is defined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by an AtkObject supporting the AtkText interface and a character offset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to it."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionProtocol"}],"title":"TextSelectionProtocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:3Atk21TextSelectionProtocolP","modules":[{"name":"Atk"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionProtocol"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol\/endObject","doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol\/endOffset","doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol\/startIsActive","doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol\/startObject","doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionProtocol\/startOffset"]}],"references":{"doc://Atk/4GLib14PointerWrapperP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"GLib.PointerWrapper","identifier":"doc:\/\/Atk\/4GLib14PointerWrapperP"},"doc://Atk/documentation/Atk/TextSelectionRef":{"role":"symbol","title":"TextSelectionRef","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionRef"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This structure represents a single  text selection within a document. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection is defined by two points in the content, where each one is defined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by an AtkObject supporting the AtkText interface and a character offset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Atk\/documentation\/Atk\/TextSelectionRef","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextSelectionRef"}],"url":"\/documentation\/atk\/textselectionref"},"doc://Atk/d